        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, flowering plants, aquatic plants, distribution\n- Products: Apium, Elodea\n- Places: Europe, Asia, Africa, South America, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Elodea was described as a genus in 1803.\n- Apium is a genus of about 20 species of flowering plants in the family Apiaceae.\n- Apium includes celery and the marshworts.\n- Apium has a subcosmopolitan distribution in Europe, Asia, Africa, South America, and Australia.\n- Elodea is a genus of 6 species of aquatic plants.\n- Elodea is often called the waterweeds.",
